From: LukeValen <panvk-eden@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 110] android: enable native Kbase release fences by default

The Eden safety path drained the entire GPU queue on every Android native
buffer release. In the stable dev.13 trace this happened 2405 times and is
a major presentation bottleneck. After fixing the 64-bit CS call address
truncation, restore native Kbase SYNC_FD export by default while retaining
PANVK_EDEN_SYNC_RELEASE=1 as an emergency synchronous fallback.

Target: Eden Android / Mali-G615 MC6 / Kbase CSF v11

diff --git a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_android.c b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_android.c
index 0f7fde4..de88bda 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_android.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_android.c
@@ -54,6 +54,7 @@
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <sys/stat.h>
 #include <errno.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
 static struct u_gralloc *_gralloc;
@@ -658,20 +659,20 @@ vk_common_QueueSignalReleaseImageANDROID(VkQueue _queue,
    if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
       return result;
 
-   /* Eden/Kbase safety mode.  Kbase does not use DRM syncobjs and the
-    * experimental KCPU SYNC_FD export path has caused a whole-device hang on
-    * the reference phone.  For the dedicated Eden build, complete the queue
-    * synchronously and hand Android an already-signaled fence (-1) instead of
-    * entering the KCPU fence-export ioctl path.  This is deliberately a
-    * correctness/stability fallback and sacrifices CPU/GPU overlap until the
-    * KCPU exporter is proven safe on-device.
+   /* Eden/Kbase performance mode.  After fixing the 64-bit CS call address
+    * truncation, use the native Kbase SYNC_FD export path by default so
+    * presentation does not drain the whole GPU queue every frame.  Keep the
+    * old fully synchronous release path as an emergency opt-in via
+    * PANVK_EDEN_SYNC_RELEASE=1 while the optimized path is validated.
     *
     * The kbase path leaves copy_sync_payloads unset (csf-v11/103), while DRM
     * PanVK keeps that callback.  That makes this condition specific to the
     * kbase logical-device path without adding PanVK-private types here.
     */
+   const char *force_sync_release = getenv("PANVK_EDEN_SYNC_RELEASE");
    if (device->physical->properties.driverID == VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_PANVK &&
-       device->copy_sync_payloads == NULL) {
+       device->copy_sync_payloads == NULL && force_sync_release &&
+       strcmp(force_sync_release, "0") != 0) {
       VkResult idle_result = device->dispatch_table.QueueWaitIdle(_queue);
       mesa_logw("[ANB-SYNC] Eden/Kbase synchronous release QueueWaitIdle=%d",
                 idle_result);
